{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793216829,"nonce":"VlM9QLOMiUFtcLR1vlWZEwSxwJQ=","title":"Caches are shared across Environments: a PR Run can poison a gated deploy Step's cache","message":"cache_key (crates/scarab-engine/src/lib.rs:1399) folds only the Project and key-file blob hashes. No ref, fork flag or Environment goes into it. A pull-request Run can save a cache entry that a deploy Step in an Environment-governed Run later restores. The approver approved a commit, but the Step runs on bytes another Run wrote.\n\nFix direction: scope cache entries by Environment (a Run with no Environment in its own namespace), or skip restore for Steps that use Environment authority (ADR-0075 §5). This is an ADR-0065 change.\n\nFound in the ADR-0075/0076 simplification audit, 2026-10-29.","files":null}]}